{
  "about": "A Mac's first click on an inactive window (docs/adr/0016-windows.mdx, decision 9): the press that activates a window reaches it marked so (protocol version 18), and only the views that take a Mac's first mouse act on it. WindowProbe (sample/WindowProbe.tsx: Bloom's SettingsLayout, its controls and drag regions Bloom's) beside PressProbe (sample/PressProbe.tsx, the `companion`: a Pressable pad, a text field). A press on an inactive window's page, its sidebar's row, its toolbar's back button or the companion's pad only activates the window: its React tree hears nothing (no touch, so nothing shows pressed), nothing is pressed, navigated or counted, and the host says it declined the first mouse; pressed again, the active window's control acts. A press on an inactive window's text field activates it and focuses the field (NSTextView's first mouse); its rail's top band moves it in one gesture; its green bubble zooms it on the first click and restores it; a hand's double click on its title area zooms it and restores it; a secondary press on the inactive companion opens its context menu at once. Each step checks the window's frame and state, what each React tree received, what each client was delivered and what each host decided, exactly. With every press delivered as an ordinary one (the compositor not marking it, or the host ignoring the mark), the declined steps fail: the pad counts a press, the sidebar navigates, React hears the page's and the back button's touches.",
